FILES YOU NEED TO WORK ON:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  
apb_mon.sv:
  Contains the APB_Monitor and APB_Checker classes.
  You will need to complete the code for both.

apb_component.sv:
  You will need to instantiate and connect the APB_Monitor

apb_env.sv:
  You will need to instantiate and connect the APB_Checker 


FILES YOU DO NOT NEED TO ALTER:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

dut/apb_dummy.sv:
  Dummy APB slave, provides non-trivial data on read cycles
  and reports all active cycles to the console.
  
apb_harness.sv:
  Test harness and test-signals interface. You will need to add
  a new clocking block and modport for monitoring the DUT

bases.sv
  Base class definitions for Transaction, Component and Channel.
  Transaction is a base class for all transaction data classes
  such as APB_Trans.  Channel is a general-purpose FIFO channel
  that carries Transaction objects from one component to another.
  Component is the component base class, as discussed in the
  classroom session, providing hierarchy and run management.

apb_classes.sv:
  Definitions of classes APB_Trans, APB_Driver, APB_Stim, APB_Env.
  These classes are all complete.
  
mem_map_apb_trans.sv:
  This file defines classes Mem_map_APB_Trans_ascending and Mem_map_APB_Trans,
  derived from APB_Trans to provide modified stimulus.  
  
  